    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d148">

                <pb facs="0245" n="145" xml:id="pg145"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">812.00/23732: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Vera Cruz</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Foster</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Vera Cruz</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-04-26T13:00:00-06:36"><hi rendition="#italic">April 26,
                                1920—1 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 5:45 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>I am informed that rebels are planning to attack Vera Cruz within a few days.
                    Local garrison has been strengthened to 600 men whose loyalty is doubtful. In
                    the event of a revolt the only possible preventive against looting would be the
                    presence of American war ships.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Foster</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
